":true,"id":"finish","read_s":10,"text":"End of the walk so far. As more buildings are built out they join it, in their place by detail and area."}],"evidence":[{"confidence":"reconstructed","id":"tour","liberty":"L-jaunt-prairie-built-so-far","sources":[],"text":"Which buildings the walk includes, their detail levels, its grouping and order, reading times and keepsake are this project's own description of its models, rewritten from the records by tools/jaunt_built_so_far.py; no historical visit is asserted."},{"confidence":"attested","id":"stood-1","locator":"HABS ILL-1015 data pages 13-15 (PDF pp. 14-16): roofs, walls, courtyard elevation, adjoining-house brick, iron-work, windows, the narrow north windows along 18th Street; p. 9 (PDF p. 10): the courtyard entrance from the alley, the Virginia creeper on the courtyard walls and the Boston ivy on the front; p. 15 (PDF p. 16): the service entrance through the great arch on Eighteenth Street.","sources":["glessner_story_of_a_house_1923","habs_glessner_house_il_1015_data_pages","inland_architect_1888_02_glessner_exterior"],"text":"1800 Prairie, the Glessner house stood on 1 July 1904, as its structure record carries it."},{"confidence":"inferred","id":"stood-2","reasoning":"STANDING IN 1904 is what the scene needs, and it rests on the 1911 Sanborn sheet 28 carried back seven years, the same reading the Glessner record and the 1904 parcels make of it (the Glessner House correspondent reads no change on this sheet between 1904 and 1911). FROM: the T-1837 building register reports 1886 (Cobb & Frost); it is not a source record here, so the day is the 1st of January and the confidence inferred. TO: the register reports the loss in 1968; same footing, the year's last day.","sources":["sanborn_1911_vol3_sheet_28","sanborn_1911_chicago_v3_sheet_28"],"text":"1808 Prairie, the Keith house stood on 1 July 1904, as its structure record carries it."},{"confidence":"inferred","id":"stood-3","reasoning":"Built for George H. Wheeler